Longlist,68,B,Safety,,"City St George's, University of London",BSc Data Science,UK,London,City strong for business/informatics; mid-ranked,QS ~#350,ABB incl Mathematics (indicative),"AAAB predicted (Maths A, Further Maths A, Chemistry A, Physics B)",Yes,IELTS 6.5 (6.0) typical,Foundation route available,GBP 24000,GBP 72000,GBP 15500,3,699150,City international undergraduate scholarships (partial) — City scholarships portal,,,,~GBP 13347/yr living shown (London rate) for Student visa,Graduate Route post-study work (currently ~2 yrs; being reduced — confirm),UK degree — MQA generally recognises; Data Science unregulated,UCAS,2027-01-15,2027 Sept,"London location, dedicated Data Science BSc, lower entry (ABB) -> SAFETY (he is well above). Cheaper tuition than the Russell Group London options but London living is high. Ranking is modest.",https://www.ucas.com/explore/courses/5f8ea4dc-e3f9-4cd3-b4d6-045fe04fc32f/course,Not verified
Longlist,79,A,Reach,Over budget,Cornell University,BA Statistical Science / BS Information Science (data science concentration),USA,"Ithaca, New York",World-leading for statistics/ORIE; Bowers College of Computing and Information Science,QS ~#16,Holistic; no fixed grade cutoff. ~7% admit. SAT/ACT REQUIRED for Fall 2026 entry onward (reinstated),"AAAB predicted (Maths A, Further Maths A, Chemistry A, Physics B)",No,IELTS 7.0 typical,No foundation route; US admission is direct-entry only,USD 71000,USD 284000,USD 21000,4,1729600,"Cornell need-based grant — CSS Profile required, via finaid.cornell.edu/first-year-and-transfer-students-international","Meets 100% of admitted international undergraduates' demonstrated need, but the package includes Cornell grants PLUS an annual work-study award AND 'reasonable student loans depending on total family income' — so it is NOT all grant, unlike Dartmouth.","Aid is guaranteed once admitted, but admission is need-AWARE for internationals: requesting aid is explicitly 'one factor amongst many' in the decision.",Complete the CSS Profile when applying for admission. Note the trade-off: asking for aid measurably lowers his admission odds here.,Family contribution after aid; full COA otherwise for the F-1 visa,F-1 OPT 12 months + 24-month STEM extension = 3 yrs; H-1B lottery thereafter,MQA generally recognises accredited US degrees; Data Science unregulated — no professional-body gate,Common App,2027-01-02,2027 Fall,"SHARPEST QUANT/TRADING FIT ON THE LIST alongside Emory QTM — Statistical Science, Information Science and ORIE are all world-class and feed directly into quant/fintech, matching his 'Trading' interest. Highest-ranked school on his US list (QS ~#16). Official finaid page confirms meets-100%-of-need for admitted internationals BUT need-AWARE admission and packages that include LOANS (not pure grant) — materially worse than Dartmouth's offer. SAT/ACT REQUIRED for Fall 2026+ (Cornell Chronicle) — no score on file.",https://finaid.cornell.edu/first-year-and-transfer-students-international,Not verified
Longlist,75,A,Reach,Over budget,Washington University in St. Louis,BS Data Science,USA,"St. Louis, Missouri",Strong CSE school; dedicated Data Science BS,QS ~#100; US News national top-25,Holistic; ~12% admit. Test-optional,"AAAB predicted (Maths A, Further Maths A, Chemistry A, Physics B)",No,IELTS 7.0 typical,No foundation route; US admission is direct-entry only,USD 68000,USD 272000,USD 21000,4,1673200,"WashU need-based aid — CSS Profile, via financialaid.washu.edu/apply-for-aid/international-applicant-process/","Official page: 'WashU is committed to meeting 100% of demonstrated financial need WITHOUT LOANS for all admitted undergraduate students' — the international applicant page states this, so grants not loans.",Meets-full-need without loans is a strong commitment; admission is the barrier. Merit scholarships also exist for internationals.,Submit the CSS Profile with the admission application by the published aid deadline. First-year international applicants ARE eligible (transfers are not).,Family contribution after aid; full COA otherwise for the F-1 visa,F-1 OPT 12 months + 24-month STEM extension = 3 yrs; H-1B lottery thereafter,MQA generally recognises accredited US degrees; Data Science unregulated — no professional-body gate,Common App,2027-01-02,2027 Fall,"BEST BALANCE OF THE NEED-AWARE TIER — a genuine dedicated BS Data Science (not a minor or an adjacent stats degree), meets 100% of need WITHOUT loans per the official international-applicant page, test-optional (so the missing SAT does not block him), and ~12% admit is the softest of the highly-ranked options. Strongest 'reachable AND well-ranked AND fully-funded' candidate. Verify need-blind vs need-aware for internationals at Stage 4 — the page states the aid commitment but not the admission posture.",https://cse.washu.edu/academics/undergraduate/BS-Data-Science.html,Not verified
Longlist,75,A,Reach,Over budget,Northwestern University,BA/BS Data Science (Department of Statistics and Data Science),USA,"Evanston, Illinois",Strong Statistics and Data Science department with a dedicated Data Science major,QS ~#50; US News national top-10,Holistic; ~7% admit. Test-optional,"AAAB predicted (Maths A, Further Maths A, Chemistry A, Physics B)",No,IELTS 7.0 typical,No foundation route; US admission is direct-entry only,USD 70000,USD 280000,USD 22000,4,1729600,Northwestern need-based aid — CSS Profile via undergradaid.northwestern.edu,Meets 100% of demonstrated need for admitted students; international applicants are eligible but the pool is limited.,Need-aware for internationals; the aid pool for non-US citizens is materially smaller than the domestic one.,Indicate aid interest on the Common App and file the CSS Profile by the round deadline.,Family contribution after aid; full COA otherwise for the F-1 visa,F-1 OPT 12 months + 24-month STEM extension = 3 yrs; H-1B lottery thereafter,MQA generally recognises accredited US degrees; Data Science unregulated — no professional-body gate,Common App,2027-01-02,2027 Fall,"A real, dedicated Data Science major confirmed from the official Northwestern catalog (11 department units + maths/ethics/domain electives), inside a top-10 US university — a strong combination of his #1 (ranking) and course fit. Test-optional helps given no SAT. Aid for internationals is need-aware and the pool is limited, so the funding is far less certain than Dartmouth/WashU. Verify the international aid posture and actual award sizes at Stage 4.",https://catalogs.northwestern.edu/undergraduate/arts-sciences/statistics-data-science/data-science-major/,Not verified
Longlist,75,A,Reach,Over budget,Duke University,BS Statistical Science,USA,"Durham, North Carolina",Statistical Science is a top-tier US department,QS ~#50; US News national top-10,"Holistic; ~6% admit overall — but aid-seeking internationals are judged in a SEPARATE, far smaller pool. Test-optional","AAAB predicted (Maths A, Further Maths A, Chemistry A, Physics B)",No,IELTS 7.0 typical,No foundation route; US admission is direct-entry only,USD 69000,USD 276000,USD 22000,4,1710800,"Karsh Office of Undergraduate Financial Support — CSS Profile, via financialaid.duke.edu/international-students/","Meets 100% of demonstrated need for eight semesters, awarded as a four-year package that auto-renews.","BRUTAL: Duke expects to enrol only 20-25 aid-receiving international students PER YEAR across the whole university. Applicants who request aid are placed in a separate, much more competitive admission pool.",MUST tick the financial-aid interest box on the admission application — students admitted having declared 'no financial aid interest' are permanently ineligible for aid in ANY undergraduate year. This is an irreversible one-way door.,Family contribution after aid; full COA otherwise for the F-1 visa,F-1 OPT 12 months + 24-month STEM extension = 3 yrs; H-1B lottery thereafter,MQA generally recognises accredited US degrees; Data Science unregulated — no professional-body gate,Common App,2027-01-02,2027 Fall,"EXCELLENT COURSE, PUNISHING ODDS. The headline ~6% admit rate badly understates the difficulty: Duke funds only 20-25 international students a year in total, and aid-seekers compete in a separate pool — so the effective admit rate for a Malaysian needing aid is far below his sub-5% deal-breaker in spirit, even though Duke's published rate clears it. Kept as an aspirational Reach, not a plan. CRITICAL PROCESS TRAP: the aid-interest box must be ticked on the original application — it cannot be added later, ever.",https://financialaid.duke.edu/international-students/,Not verified
Longlist,75,A,Reach,Over budget,Brown University,BS Applied Mathematics-Computer Science / Data Science,USA,"Providence, Rhode Island",Strong Applied Maths + Data Science Initiative,QS ~#60; Ivy League,Holistic; ~5.2% admit — ABOVE his 5% cutoff but only just. SAT/ACT REQUIRED (reinstated for Fall 2025 onward),"AAAB predicted (Maths A, Further Maths A, Chemistry A, Physics B)",No,IELTS 7.0 typical,No foundation route; US admission is direct-entry only,USD 71000,USD 284000,USD 21000,4,1729600,Brown need-based aid — CSS Profile via financialaid.brown.edu,"Meets 100% of demonstrated need; need-blind for international applicants beginning with the Class of 2029, which covers a 2027 entry.",Aid guaranteed once admitted and need-blind — but the ~5.2% admit rate is the tightest on his list.,Indicate aid interest and file the CSS Profile by the round deadline.,Family contribution after aid; full COA otherwise for the F-1 visa,F-1 OPT 12 months + 24-month STEM extension = 3 yrs; H-1B lottery thereafter,MQA generally recognises accredited US degrees; Data Science unregulated — no professional-body gate,Common App,2027-01-01,2027 Fall,"DELIBERATELY BORDERLINE ON HIS OWN DEAL-BREAKER — Brown's ~5.2% admit clears the sub-5% cutoff, but only just, and the rate moves year to year. Flagging rather than silently including or excluding it: if the published rate dips below 5% for the 2027 cycle it must be dropped per his stated rule. Need-blind for internationals from the Class of 2029 + meets full need makes the funding excellent. SAT/ACT REQUIRED — no score on file. Brown's Open Curriculum suits an undecided student.",https://www.brown.edu/academics/data-science/,Not verified
Longlist,72,B,Reach,Over budget,Dartmouth College,BA Quantitative Social Science (QSS) / Computer Science,USA,"Hanover, New Hampshire",Ivy League; QSS is a niche but well-regarded quantitative programme,QS ~#200; US News national top-15,Holistic; no fixed grade cutoff. ~6% admit. SAT/ACT REQUIRED (test-optional policy reversed for Fall 2025 onward),"AAAB predicted (Maths A, Further Maths A, Chemistry A, Physics B)",No,IELTS ~7.0 typical (no fixed minimum published),No foundation route; US admission is direct-entry only,USD 70000,USD 280000,USD 22000,4,1729600,"Need-based Dartmouth scholarship (grant, never repaid) — apply via CSS Profile alongside the Common App at financialaid.dartmouth.edu/apply-aid/international-students","Meets 100% of demonstrated need; loans eliminated from packages. Award scales to assessed family need, not to the sticker price.","Aid itself is guaranteed once admitted — the competition is the ~6% admission, not the money. Funded by a $40m gift specifically to make international admission need-blind.","Indicate aid interest on the Common App and submit the CSS Profile by the admission-round deadline. Because Dartmouth is need-blind for all international citizens, asking for aid does NOT reduce his admission odds.",Reduced to the family contribution once aid is awarded; full COA shown otherwise for the F-1 visa,F-1 OPT 12 months + 24-month STEM extension = 3 yrs (QSS/CS are STEM-designated); H-1B lottery thereafter,MQA generally recognises accredited US degrees; Data Science unregulated — no professional-body gate,Common App,2027-01-01,2027 Fall,"THE BEST STRUCTURAL FIT FOR HIS FUNDING SITUATION. Need-BLIND for all international citizens since the Class of 2026 (official page confirms) + meets 100% of need with no loans — so applying for aid costs him nothing in admission odds. This is the rare case where the aid is guaranteed and only admission is the barrier. TWO CAVEATS: (1) SAT/ACT is REQUIRED — he has no score on file and must sit it by ~Nov 2026. (2) QSS is quantitative social science, not a pure Data Science degree — CS is the closer fit. Verify the exact major at Stage 4.",https://admissions.dartmouth.edu/apply-dartmouth/universal-need-blind-policy,Not verified
Longlist,72,B,Reach,Over budget,Emory University,BS Quantitative Sciences (QTM — Quantitative Theory and Methods),USA,"Atlanta, Georgia","QTM is a distinctive, well-regarded applied data-science department",QS ~#150; US News national top-25,Holistic; ~11% admit. Test-optional,"AAAB predicted (Maths A, Further Maths A, Chemistry A, Physics B)",No,IELTS 7.0 typical,No foundation route; US admission is direct-entry only,USD 65000,USD 260000,USD 20000,4,1598000,Emory need-based aid for internationals + Emory University Scholar Programs (merit) — CSS Profile via studentaid.emory.edu/undergraduate/apply/new-students/international.html,Need-based awards to 'a select group of international applicants each year' — NOT a meets-full-need guarantee for internationals. Emory Scholars (merit) can be full tuition.,"Two separate shots: a limited need-based pool AND the Emory Scholars merit programme, for which internationals are eligible. The merit route is the more realistic one for a family-funded applicant.",Must apply REGULAR DECISION to be considered for need-based aid; complete the CSS Profile before 5 February. Apply separately/early for Emory Scholars.,Family contribution after aid; full COA otherwise for the F-1 visa,F-1 OPT 12 months + 24-month STEM extension = 3 yrs; H-1B lottery thereafter,MQA generally recognises accredited US degrees; Data Science unregulated — no professional-body gate,Common App,2027-01-01,2027 Fall,"SHARPEST COURSE FIT FOR THE 'TRADING' HINT alongside Cornell — QTM is effectively an applied data-science major built around statistical modelling of real-world/economic data, and it is one of the few US undergrad departments purpose-built for this. Test-optional, so the missing SAT does not block him. WEAKER AID than the meets-full-need tier: need-based goes to 'a select group' only, so the merit route (Emory Scholars) is the realistic play. NOTE: must apply Regular Decision to be eligible for need-based aid — this conflicts with using Early Decision to boost admission odds.",https://quantitative.emory.edu/,Not verified
Longlist,72,B,Reach,Over budget,Vanderbilt University,BS Data Science,USA,"Nashville, Tennessee",Data Science Institute; undergraduate Data Science major,QS ~#150; US News national top-20,Holistic; ~6% admit. Test-optional,"AAAB predicted (Maths A, Further Maths A, Chemistry A, Physics B)",No,IELTS 7.0 typical,No foundation route; US admission is direct-entry only,USD 66000,USD 264000,USD 21000,4,1635600,Need-based scholarships for internationals (CSS Profile or ISFAA) + Cornelius Vanderbilt Scholarship (merit) — admissions.vanderbilt.edu/affordability/international-costs-and-finances/,"Official page: need-based scholarships to 'a limited number' of first-year internationals; the range of awards offered was USD 24,587-97,566 per year for four years — the top of that range is a full ride.","Need-AWARE for aid-seeking internationals, who are pooled and ranked against each other on academics, leadership and financial need. The Cornelius Vanderbilt merit route is strongly encouraged as a parallel shot.",Submit the CSS Profile or ISFAA; apply separately for the Cornelius Vanderbilt Scholarship. NOTE: no need-based aid at all for international TRANSFER applicants.,Family contribution after aid; full COA otherwise for the F-1 visa,F-1 OPT 12 months + 24-month STEM extension = 3 yrs; H-1B lottery thereafter,MQA generally recognises accredited US degrees; Data Science unregulated — no professional-body gate,Common App,2027-01-01,2027 Fall,"DUAL FUNDING ROUTE (need-based + Cornelius Vanderbilt merit) and a real undergraduate Data Science major, which is a good structural fit. The official international page confirms awards ranging USD 24,587-97,566/yr — so a full ride is genuinely possible, but only for a limited number and on a need-AWARE basis. CAUTION FOR STAGE 4: vanderbilt.edu/datascience is the Data Science Institute (MASTER'S) site — its '25%-100% of tuition' scholarships are for the MS, NOT the undergraduate degree. Do not carry that figure into an undergrad row.",https://admissions.vanderbilt.edu/affordability/international-costs-and-finances/,Not verified
Longlist,70,B,Reach,Over budget,Amherst College,BA Statistics,USA,"Amherst, Massachusetts",Elite US liberal-arts college; dedicated Statistics department (est. 2025),Not ranked in QS (liberal-arts colleges are excluded); US News #1-3 national liberal arts,Holistic; ~7% admit. Test-optional,"AAAB predicted (Maths A, Further Maths A, Chemistry A, Physics B)",No,IELTS 7.0 typical,No foundation route; US admission is direct-entry only,USD 71000,USD 284000,USD 20000,4,1710800,Amherst need-based aid — CSS Profile via amherst.edu/admission/financialaid,Meets 100% of calculated need for all admitted international students who apply for aid; no-loan packages.,"Aid guaranteed once admitted; Amherst admits internationals WITHOUT regard to financial need (fully need-blind), so requesting aid is free.",Indicate aid interest and file the CSS Profile by the round deadline.,Family contribution after aid; full COA otherwise for the F-1 visa,F-1 OPT 12 months + 24-month STEM extension = 3 yrs (Statistics is STEM-designated); H-1B lottery thereafter,MQA generally recognises accredited US degrees; Data Science unregulated. NOTE: liberal-arts colleges have low name-recognition with Malaysian employers despite elite US standing,Common App,2027-01-01,2027 Fall,"BEST-FUNDED OF THE LIBERAL-ARTS OPTIONS and the only one with a real Statistics major (department launched 2025). Fully need-blind for internationals + meets 100% of need. Test-optional, so no SAT block. THE HONEST TENSION: Amherst is elite in the US but invisible in QS and largely unknown to Malaysian employers — it scores poorly on his #1 priority (ranking) and on recognition back home, despite being, on funding and teaching, one of the strongest options here. Worth a direct conversation about whether 'the name' means QS rank or US reputation.",https://www.amherst.edu/academiclife/departments/statistics,Not verified
Longlist,69,B,Reach,Over budget,University of Notre Dame,BS Applied and Computational Mathematics and Statistics (ACMS),USA,"Notre Dame, Indiana",ACMS is a solid applied maths/statistics/data-analysis department,QS ~#200; US News national top-20,Holistic; ~12% admit. Test-optional,"AAAB predicted (Maths A, Further Maths A, Chemistry A, Physics B)",No,IELTS 7.0 typical,No foundation route; US admission is direct-entry only,USD 66000,USD 264000,USD 20000,4,1616800,Notre Dame need-based aid — CSS Profile via financialaid.nd.edu,Meets 100% of demonstrated need; need-blind for international applicants beginning with the Class of 2029 — which covers a 2027 entry (Class of 2031).,"Aid guaranteed once admitted, and need-blind means requesting it does not hurt his odds. ~12% admit is one of the softer gates among need-blind schools.",Indicate aid interest and file the CSS Profile by the round deadline.,Family contribution after aid; full COA otherwise for the F-1 visa,F-1 OPT 12 months + 24-month STEM extension = 3 yrs; H-1B lottery thereafter,MQA generally recognises accredited US degrees; Data Science unregulated — no professional-body gate,Common App,2027-01-01,2027 Fall,"THE MOST REACHABLE NEED-BLIND OPTION. Notre Dame joined the need-blind-for-internationals list from the Class of 2029, so a 2027 entrant qualifies — combined with ~12% admit (double Dartmouth's) and test-optional, this is the softest gate at which the aid is still guaranteed AND asking for it is free. ACMS BS is a real applied-maths/stats degree (confirmed from the official department page) though not branded 'Data Science'. Strongly Catholic campus culture — worth flagging to him as a fit question, not a defect. Verify the Class-of-2029 need-blind start date at Stage 4.",https://acms.nd.edu/undergraduate/,Not verified
Longlist,69,B,Reach,Over budget,Rice University,BS Statistics / Data Science,USA,"Houston, Texas",Strong statistics and computational science; consistently rated a best-value private,QS ~#100; US News national top-20,Holistic; ~8% admit. Test-optional,"AAAB predicted (Maths A, Further Maths A, Chemistry A, Physics B)",No,IELTS 7.0 typical,No foundation route; US admission is direct-entry only,USD 71140,USD 284560,USD 20530,4,1723396,Rice need-based aid — CSS Profile via financialaid.rice.edu/apply-aid/international-students,Official page: need-based aid to 'a LIMITED NUMBER of international first-year applicants' — no meets-full-need guarantee for internationals.,"Limited pool. For context the official COA page gives an average freshman aid package of USD 75,643 and an average family responsibility of USD 16,819 — but those are all-student figures, not international-specific.",Submit the CSS Profile with the admission application; internationals compete for a small allocation.,Family contribution after aid; full COA otherwise for the F-1 visa,F-1 OPT 12 months + 24-month STEM extension = 3 yrs; H-1B lottery thereafter,MQA generally recognises accredited US degrees; Data Science unregulated — no professional-body gate,Common App,2027-01-01,2027 Fall,"HARD 2026-27 COST DATA scraped from Rice's official page: tuition USD 71,140 + fees 984 + on-campus living 20,530 => TOTAL COA USD 97,309/yr (~1.83M MYR over 4 yrs at sticker). This is the most reliable cost figure on the whole US list and a useful yardstick for what a US private actually costs. Aid is the weak point: 'a limited number' of internationals only, so the funding is a lottery within a lottery. Test-optional.",https://financialaid.rice.edu/cost-attendance,Not verified
Longlist,66,B,Reach,Over budget,Carnegie Mellon University,BS Statistics and Machine Learning / Computational Data Science,USA,"Pittsburgh, Pennsylvania",World top-5 for computer science and data science,QS ~#50; US News CS #1,Holistic; ~11% overall but the School of Computer Science is far tighter (~5%). SAT/ACT required for some colleges,"AAAB predicted (Maths A, Further Maths A, Chemistry A, Physics B)",No,IELTS 7.5 typical (CMU sets a high bar),No foundation route; US admission is direct-entry only,USD 68000,USD 272000,USD 20000,4,1654400,NONE available to him — CMU awards no need-based institutional aid to international undergraduates,Zero. CMU does not award need-based aid to international undergrads (only DACA students and a small number from specific partner countries).,Not applicable — he is ineligible.,"No route. The full ~USD 88,000/yr would be payable from family funds.","Full COA (~USD 88,000/yr) must be shown for the F-1 visa",F-1 OPT 12 months + 24-month STEM extension = 3 yrs; H-1B lottery thereafter,MQA generally recognises accredited US degrees; Data Science unregulated — no professional-body gate,Common App,2027-01-01,2027 Fall,"KEPT DELIBERATELY AS A NEGATIVE FINDING, not as a recommendation (same treatment as Toru's CMU row). On pure course and reputation CMU is arguably the best data-science destination on earth, so its absence would look like an oversight — but it awards NO need-based aid to international undergraduates, which makes it a ~1.65M MYR full-freight commitment, roughly double his ceiling. It is on the list so the trade-off is visible and he can rule it out himself, with reasons.",https://www.cmu.edu/,Not verified
Longlist,61,B,Reach,Over budget,University of Richmond,BS Mathematics / Computer Science with the Data Science & Statistics minor,USA,"Richmond, Virginia","Well-regarded small private; data science is a MINOR, not a major",Not ranked in QS; US News ~top-25 national liberal arts,"Holistic; ~22% admit overall — but need-aware for internationals, so the aid-seeking rate is lower. Test-optional","AAAB predicted (Maths A, Further Maths A, Chemistry A, Physics B)",No,IELTS 7.0 typical,No foundation route; US admission is direct-entry only,USD 66000,USD 264000,USD 16000,4,1541600,Richmond need-based aid + merit scholarships (Richmond Scholars) — financialaid.richmond.edu/applying/international.html,"Official page: 'committed to meeting the FULL demonstrated financial need of all admitted domestic and international applicants'. Average total aid award to internationals in 2025-26 was USD 69,900. Grants and merit run for eight semesters.",Need-AWARE: 'a student's ability to pay for four years will be considered during the admission review'. Internationals get full consideration for merit scholarships too (except Army ROTC).,Submit the Certification of Financial Responsibility (required for all non-US citizens) plus the need-based aid forms. Apply by the 1 DECEMBER Richmond Scholars deadline for full merit eligibility — earlier than the regular round.,Family contribution after aid; full COA otherwise for the F-1 visa,F-1 OPT 12 months + 24-month STEM extension = 3 yrs; H-1B lottery thereafter,MQA generally recognises accredited US degrees; Data Science unregulated. NOTE: low name-recognition with Malaysian employers,Common App,2026-12-01,2027 Fall,"THE SOFTEST ADMISSION GATE ON THE US LIST THAT STILL MEETS FULL NEED — ~22% admit and an official meets-full-need-for-internationals commitment, with an average international award of USD 69,900 (verified on their aid page) that would cover most of the sticker. Lower living costs too. TWO REAL WEAKNESSES: (1) data science is only a MINOR — he would major in Maths or CS, so course fit is compromised; (2) no QS ranking and little recognition in Malaysia, hitting his #1 priority hard. DEADLINE IS EARLY: 1 December 2026 for full scholarship consideration, a month before the Common App norm.",https://datascience.richmond.edu/,Not verified
Longlist,60,B,Reach,Over budget,Grinnell College,BA Computer Science / Mathematics (statistics and data-science coursework),USA,"Grinnell, Iowa",Liberal-arts college with an unusually strong CS department and a large endowment per student,Not ranked in QS; US News ~top-15 national liberal arts,Holistic; ~11% admit. Test-optional,"AAAB predicted (Maths A, Further Maths A, Chemistry A, Physics B)",No,IELTS 7.0 typical,No foundation route; US admission is direct-entry only,USD 70000,USD 280000,USD 18000,4,1654400,Grinnell need-based aid + merit — CSS Profile via grinnell.edu/admission/apply/international,Official page: 'a full range of financial aid opportunities to international students... committed to providing affordable education'. Grinnell is among the most generous LACs to internationals but is need-aware.,"Generous relative to peers thanks to a very large per-student endowment, but need-aware for internationals.",File the CSS Profile with the admission application.,Family contribution after aid; full COA otherwise for the F-1 visa,F-1 OPT 12 months + 24-month STEM extension = 3 yrs; H-1B lottery thereafter,MQA generally recognises accredited US degrees; Data Science unregulated. NOTE: very low name-recognition with Malaysian employers,Common App,2027-01-01,2027 Fall,"Included as a genuinely aid-generous, moderately-reachable option (~11%) with a CS department far stronger than its size suggests. No dedicated data-science major — he'd major in CS or Maths. Same structural problem as the other LACs: excellent funding and teaching, near-zero brand recognition in Malaysia, no QS rank — so it scores badly on his #1 priority. Rural Iowa; he ticked Rural/Campus-based as acceptable, so location is not a blocker.",https://www.grinnell.edu/admission/apply/international,Not verified
Shortlist,87,A,Safety,,University of Melbourne,Bachelor of Science (Data Science major),Australia,Melbourne,QS Data Science & AI 2026 #31 (highest in Australia),QS ~#13,GCE A Level AAB (Melbourne quotes AAB for its IT/Data Science degree package); guaranteed entry ATAR 91.00; Units 3&4 maths prerequisite,"AAAB predicted (Maths A, Further Maths A, Chemistry A, Physics B)",Yes,IELTS 6.5 overall (6.0 each band),Trinity College Foundation Studies if below AAB,AUD 49188,AUD 147564,AUD 31000,3,745748,"Melbourne International Undergraduate Scholarship — automatic consideration, NO application required",25% fee remission for the duration of the course,At least 110 awarded; automatic consideration on academic merit,No application — all international undergraduate applicants are considered automatically on admission,"AUD 29,710/yr living costs + first-year tuition + return airfare (subclass 500, 2026 figure)","485 Temporary Graduate visa, Post-Higher-Education Work stream — 2 yrs for a bachelor",MQA recognised; strong Malaysian employer recognition; no professional-body gate for Data Science,Direct to University of Melbourne (international),,2027 Semester 2 (late July) — or Semester 1 (Feb 2027) if A-Level results land in time,"Australia's best-ranked data science option and the strongest single row on his #1 priority. Data Science is a MAJOR inside the BSc, not a dedicated degree — he picks it from year 2, so year 1 is broad science. The 25% automatic fee remission is the best scholarship structure found in Australia: no application, no competition to enter. Fee is subject-based not course-based, so the total moves with subject choice. VERIFY the A Level AAB figure at Stage 4 — it comes from Melbourne's graduate-degree-package page, not the BSc entry page.",https://study.unimelb.edu.au/find/courses/undergraduate/bachelor-of-science/,Not verified
Longlist,85,A,Safety,,Monash University,Bachelor of Applied Data Science,Australia,Melbourne (Clayton),QS Data Science & AI 2026 — 5th in Australia (Monash claims #5 nationally),QS ~#36,Australian Year 12 or equivalent; prerequisite higher-level Mathematics; indicative ATAR low-to-mid 80s,"AAAB predicted (Maths A, Further Maths A) — maths prerequisite comfortably met",Yes,IELTS 6.5 overall (6.0 each band),Monash College Diploma; also transferable from Monash Malaysia,AUD 45600,AUD 136800,AUD 31000,3,712380,Monash International Merit Scholarship + 360 other scholarship types,"Varies; Monash advertises scholarships valued up to A$280,000","Merit-based, competitive",Apply via the Monash scholarships portal alongside/after the course application,"AUD 29,710/yr living costs + first-year tuition + return airfare (subclass 500, 2026 figure)","485 Temporary Graduate visa, Post-Higher-Education Work stream — 2 yrs for a bachelor",MQA recognised; very strong Malaysian employer recognition (Monash Malaysia campus is well known at home),Direct to Monash (international),,2027 Semester 2 (July) — Semester 1 (Feb 2027) also offered at Clayton,"Best desirability-per-ringgit among the well-ranked options: a dedicated data science degree, 5th in Australia for DS&AI, ~712k MYR total — inside his ceiling with room. The Clayton course is also offered at Monash Malaysia, which opens a cheaper 'start at home, transfer' route worth raising with him (his profile allows Malaysia in scope). Fee A$45,600 is per 48 credit points = one standard full-time year.",https://www.monash.edu/study/courses/find-a-course/applied-data-science-s2010,Not verified
Shortlist,80,A,Safety,Over budget,University of New South Wales,Bachelor of Data Science and Decisions,Australia,Sydney,"QS Data Science & AI 2026 — ranked, below Monash/UTS in Australia",QS ~#19,"2026 A Levels entry score 13.0 (aggregate of best 3-4 A2 subjects, A*=6 A=5 B=4 C=3 D=2 E=1); 2026 Lowest ATAR 81.8; Lowest Selection Rank 90.0",AAAB predicted = aggregate 19 of best four (15 of best three) — well above the 13.0 cutoff,Yes,IELTS 6.5 overall (6.0 each band),UNSW College Diploma if below cutoff,AUD 60000,AUD 189000,AUD 31000,3,874200,"UNSW International Scholarships — competitive, partial",Typically partial fee remission,Competitive; no meets-full-need equivalent,Apply via the UNSW scholarships portal after receiving an offer,"AUD 29,710/yr living costs + first-year tuition + return airfare (subclass 500, 2026 figure)","485 Temporary Graduate visa, Post-Higher-Education Work stream — 2 yrs for a bachelor",MQA recognised; strong Malaysian employer recognition; no professional-body gate for Data Science,Direct to UNSW (international) / UAC,,2027 Semester 2 (late July) — or Term 1 (Feb 2027) if A-Level results land in time,"THE CLEAREST ADMISSIBILITY WIN ON HIS WHOLE LIST. UNSW publishes an explicit A-Level cutoff of 13.0 and his AAAB scores 19 — a 6-point margin at a QS ~#19 university. This is the well-ranked Safety the US round could not produce. The 'decisions' framing (statistics + econometrics + optimisation) is the closest fit found to his trading interest. COST TRAP: the page shows A$8,500/yr and A$27,000 total right next to the international figures — those are the domestic Commonwealth Supported Place rates and do NOT apply to him; the international total is A$189,000. That drives it just over his 800k ceiling.",https://www.unsw.edu.au/study/undergraduate/bachelor-of-data-science-and-decisions,Not verified
Shortlist,78,A,Match,Over budget,University of Sydney,Bachelor of Advanced Computing (Computer Science / Data Science major),Australia,Sydney,QS Data Science & AI 2026 #38,QS ~#18,Indicative ATAR 95+ for Advanced Computing; A Level equivalent around AAA,AAAB predicted — borderline against an AAA-equivalent bar,Yes,IELTS 6.5 overall (6.0 each band),Taylors College Sydney foundation; or the 3-yr Bachelor of Science (Data Science major) as a cheaper sibling,AUD 53500,AUD 214000,AUD 31000,4,1047800,Sydney International Student Award / Vice-Chancellor's International Scholarships,Typically partial fee remission,Highly competitive,Apply via the Sydney scholarships portal,"AUD 29,710/yr living costs + first-year tuition + return airfare (subclass 500, 2026 figure)","485 Temporary Graduate visa, Post-Higher-Education Work stream — 2 yrs for a bachelor",MQA recognised; strong Malaysian employer recognition,Direct to University of Sydney (international) / UAC,,2027 Semester 2 (Aug) — Semester 1 (Feb 2027) also offered,"THE 3-VS-4-YEAR TRAP IN ONE ROW. Advanced Computing is a FOUR-year degree, so at ~1.05M MYR it costs more than Melbourne and Monash combined-per-year despite a similar annual fee — the extra year, not the fee, is what busts the budget. Sydney's own course page would not show a tuition figure for the selected year (the A$53,500 is from aggregators — verify). If he wants Sydney, the 3-year BSc with a data science major is the row to discover at Stage 4; this one is kept to make the duration cost visible rather than hidden.",https://www.sydney.edu.au/courses/courses/uc/bachelor-of-advanced-computing.html,Not verified
Longlist,77,A,Safety,,Australian National University,Bachelor of Applied Data Analytics,Australia,Canberra,QS Data Science & AI 2026 #44,QS ~#32,Minimum selection rank 90.00; Australian Year 12 or international equivalent,"AAAB predicted (Maths A, Further Maths A, Chemistry A, Physics B)",Yes,IELTS 6.5 overall (6.0 each band),ANU College foundation/diploma if below the selection rank,AUD 56120,AUD 168360,AUD 29710,3,798219,ANU International Undergraduate Scholarship / ANU Chancellor's International Scholarship,Typically 25-50% fee remission,Competitive; automatic consideration for some,Most ANU international scholarships assess on admission — check whether a separate form is needed,"AUD 29,710/yr living costs + first-year tuition + return airfare (subclass 500, 2026 figure)","485 Temporary Graduate visa, Post-Higher-Education Work stream — 2 yrs for a bachelor",MQA recognised; strong Malaysian employer recognition,Direct to ANU (international) / UAC International,,2027 Semester 2 (July) — Semester 1 (Feb 2027) also offered,"THE RAZOR-EDGE ROW: ~798k MYR total against an 800k ceiling — it clears by roughly 1,800 MYR, which is inside the rounding error of an approximate FX rate. Treat it as effectively AT budget, not under; any fee rise or a weaker ringgit tips it over. The A$56,120 annual fee is taken from the ANU Applied Data Analytics (Honours) page — VERIFY the 3-year bachelor's own fee at Stage 4, and beware that aggregators quote ~A$12,240/yr for this program, which is a domestic/per-course figure and flatly wrong for an international student.",https://programsandcourses.anu.edu.au/program/BADAN,Not verified
Longlist,77,A,Safety,,RMIT University,Bachelor of Data Science (BP340),Australia,Melbourne,QS Data Science & AI 2026 — ranked in band,QS ~#123,VCE equivalent; maths prerequisite (study score 20+ in General/Methods/Specialist Maths); no explicit A-Level threshold published,"AAAB predicted (Maths A, Further Maths A) — maths prerequisite far exceeded",Yes,IELTS 6.5 overall (6.0 each band),RMIT Foundation Studies; a Bachelor of Data Science (Professional) variant (BP348) adds a paid industry year,AUD 43200,AUD 129600,AUD 31000,3,690060,RMIT International Excellence Scholarship,Typically 20-30% fee remission,"Merit-based, moderately competitive",Apply via the RMIT scholarships portal after an offer,"AUD 29,710/yr living costs + first-year tuition + return airfare (subclass 500, 2026 figure)","485 Temporary Graduate visa, Post-Higher-Education Work stream — 2 yrs for a bachelor",MQA recognised; RMIT is well known in Malaysia (long-standing pathway partnerships),Direct to RMIT (international),,2027 Semester 2 (July) — Semester 1 (Feb 2027) also offered,"A$43,200 is the OFFICIAL 2026 international annual fee taken from RMIT's own course page — one of the few fee figures this round that is not an aggregator estimate. Dedicated 3-year data science degree, ~690k MYR total, comfortable inside budget, entry bar low against his grades. RMIT publishes no A-Level threshold for internationals; the entry_margin of +2 is inferred from the VCE prerequisite being a maths study score of 20, which he clears by a wide margin. The BP348 'Professional' variant with a paid industry placement is worth surfacing to him.",https://www.rmit.edu.au/study-with-us/levels-of-study/undergraduate-study/bachelor-degrees/bachelor-of-data-science-bp340,Not verified
Longlist,76,A,Safety,,University of Queensland,Bachelor of Mathematics (Data Science major),Australia,Brisbane,QS Data Science & AI 2026 — ranked in band,QS ~#42,GCE A Level aggregate of best 3 subjects (A*=6 A=5 B=4 C=3 D=2 E=1); UQ publishes a GCE information sheet,"AAAB predicted = aggregate 15 of best three (Maths A, Further Maths A, Chemistry A)",Yes,IELTS 6.5 overall (6.0 each band),UQ College foundation year,AUD 47000,AUD 141000,AUD 29710,3,713403,UQ International Scholarships / Global Leaders Scholarship,Typically partial fee remission,Competitive,Apply via the UQ scholarships portal,"AUD 29,710/yr living costs + first-year tuition + return airfare (subclass 500, 2026 figure)","485 Temporary Graduate visa, Post-Higher-Education Work stream — 2 yrs for a bachelor",MQA recognised; strong Malaysian employer recognition,Direct to UQ (international),,2027 Semester 2 (July) — Semester 1 (Feb 2027) also offered,"UQ uses the same A-Level aggregate scale as UNSW but counts the BEST THREE, so his Further Maths does real work here (15 of a possible 18). Maths-led rather than a dedicated DS degree — heavier theory, lighter engineering, which suits the quant/trading interest. The A$47,000 fee is a mid-range estimate from the UQ international fee band (A$30-45k+ quoted by aggregators, unreliable) — VERIFY on the UQ fee schedule at Stage 4.",https://study.uq.edu.au/study-options/programs/bachelor-mathematics-2460,Not verified
Longlist,76,A,Safety,,Queensland University of Technology,Bachelor of Data Science (Data and Decision Analytics),Australia,Brisbane,QS Data Science & AI 2026 — QUT claims top 13 in Australia / top 200 world,QS ~#189,"ATAR / selection rank 80.00 (lowest adjusted offer, Semester 1 2026); recommends English and Mathematical Methods","AAAB predicted (Maths A, Further Maths A, Chemistry A, Physics B)",Yes,IELTS 6.5 overall (6.0 each band),QUT College foundation; also a Bachelor of Business/Bachelor of Data Science double,AUD 36800,AUD 110400,AUD 29710,3,618543,QUT International Merit Scholarship,Typically 25% fee remission,Merit-based,Automatic consideration for some; others via the QUT scholarships portal,"AUD 29,710/yr living costs + first-year tuition + return airfare (subclass 500, 2026 figure)","485 Temporary Graduate visa, Post-Higher-Education Work stream — 2 yrs for a bachelor",MQA recognised; moderate Malaysian employer recognition,Direct to QUT (international) / QTAC,,2027 Semester 2 (July) — Semester 1 (Feb 2027) also offered,"The cheapest well-structured dedicated DS degree found (~619k MYR total, ~180k under his ceiling) with a published selection rank of 80 he clears easily. QUT's 'top 13 in Australia / top 200 world for DS&AI' claim is its own marketing — the QS subject table puts it in an unscored band, so treat the subject rank as weaker than QUT states. The 'Data and Decision Analytics' major is the trading-adjacent one; there is also an AI/Machine Learning major at the same cutoff.",https://www.qut.edu.au/courses/bachelor-of-data-science,Not verified
Longlist,75,A,Safety,,Macquarie University,Bachelor of Information Technology (Data Science major),Australia,Sydney,QS Data Science & AI 2026 — ranked in band,QS ~#130,Australian Year 12 or equivalent; A Levels accepted; indicative ATAR mid-to-high 70s,"AAAB predicted (Maths A, Further Maths A, Chemistry A, Physics B)",Yes,IELTS 6.5 overall (6.0 each band),Macquarie University College diploma,AUD 33535,AUD 100605,AUD 31000,3,600176,Macquarie Vice-Chancellor's International Scholarship,"Typically A$10,000/yr or partial remission",Automatic consideration on admission for some awards,Most assess automatically; check the Macquarie scholarships portal,"AUD 29,710/yr living costs + first-year tuition + return airfare (subclass 500, 2026 figure)","485 Temporary Graduate visa, Post-Higher-Education Work stream — 2 yrs for a bachelor",MQA recognised; moderate Malaysian employer recognition,Direct to Macquarie (international) / UAC,,2027 Semester 2 (July) — Semester 1 (Feb 2027) also offered,"THE CHEAPEST ROW IN SYDNEY (~600k MYR total) and the cheapest Australian option overall — a full 200k under his ceiling, which is the only thing on his entire 39-row list that leaves real headroom for a weaker ringgit or a fee rise. Data Science is a major inside a BIT, so it is IT-led rather than maths-led — a weaker fit for the quant/trading angle than UNSW or UQ. Note the A$16,000-23,500 commencement deposit is deducted FROM first-session tuition, not added to it.",https://www.mq.edu.au/study/find-a-course/courses/bachelor-of-information-technology,Not verified
Longlist,73,B,Safety,Over budget,University of Technology Sydney,Bachelor of Engineering (Honours) Data Science,Australia,Sydney,QS Data Science & AI 2026 — 4th in Australia (ahead of Monash and UNSW on subject score),QS ~#88,Indicative ATAR mid-to-high 80s; recommends Mathematics Extension 1 and Physics,"AAAB predicted (Maths A, Further Maths A, Physics B) — matches the recommended subject profile exactly",Yes,IELTS 6.5 overall (6.0 each band),UTS College diploma,AUD 48560,AUD 194240,AUD 31000,4,986544,UTS International Undergraduate Scholarships,Typically partial fee remission,Competitive,Apply via the UTS scholarships portal,"AUD 29,710/yr living costs + first-year tuition + return airfare (subclass 500, 2026 figure)","485 Temporary Graduate visa, Post-Higher-Education Work stream — 2 yrs for a bachelor","MQA recognised; accredited by Engineers Australia at Professional Engineer level and recognised under the WASHINGTON ACCORD — genuine, though Data Science is not a regulated profession so it is a bonus, not a gate",Direct to UTS (international) / UAC,,2027 Semester 2 (July) — Semester 1 (Feb 2027) also offered,"THE RANKING SURPRISE: UTS scores 4th in Australia for QS Data Science & AI (76.9) — ahead of Monash (76.3) and UNSW — despite an overall QS rank near #88. This is exactly the subject-vs-overall-rank split his weights are built for (subject_reputation 0.18 is scored on the subject, not vanity rank), and it is worth showing him explicitly because 'the name' question cuts the other way here. Cost is the catch: it is UTS's only undergraduate data science route and it is a FOUR-year engineering degree (~987k MYR), including a compulsory 12 weeks of industry experience. Washington Accord accreditation is real but buys him nothing specific in an unregulated field.",https://www.uts.edu.au/courses/bachelor-of-engineering-honours-data-science,Not verified
Longlist,72,B,Safety,,University of Wollongong,Bachelor of Data Science and Analytics,Australia,Wollongong,QS Data Science & AI 2026 — not separately ranked,QS ~#167,ATAR-SR 65 for the sibling Computational Technology degree; GCE A-Levels explicitly accepted,"AAAB predicted (Maths A, Further Maths A, Chemistry A, Physics B) — far above the published bar",Yes,IELTS 6.5 overall (6.0 each band),UOW College diploma; UOW also runs Early Admission,AUD 36672,AUD 110016,AUD 29710,3,617353,UOW International Merit / Vice-Chancellor's Scholarship,Typically 20-30% fee remission,Automatic consideration for some awards,Most assess automatically on admission,"AUD 29,710/yr living costs + first-year tuition + return airfare (subclass 500, 2026 figure)","485 Temporary Graduate visa — 2 yrs for a bachelor; Wollongong is a designated regional area, which can add an extra year",MQA recognised; weaker Malaysian employer recognition than the Go8,Direct to UOW (international) / UAC,,2027 Autumn (Feb) or Spring (July) — no Sept intake,"HIS FLOOR — the safest admissible row on the list: UOW publishes an ATAR-SR of 65 on the sibling Computational Technology degree, which his AAAB clears by a mile, and it explicitly accepts GCE A-Levels. ~617k MYR total. Regional designation is a real plus for his migration intent (possible third year on the 485). The trade-off is blunt: it is his weakest row on subject reputation, his #1 priority, so it earns its place as insurance rather than as a target. The A$36,672 fee is the quoted Computer Science figure — verify the DS&A course fee specifically at Stage 4.",https://www.uow.edu.au/study/courses/bachelor-of-data-science-and-analytics/,Not verified
Longlist,70,B,Safety,,Adelaide University,Bachelor of Mathematical Sciences (Data Science),Australia,Adelaide,QS Data Science & AI 2026 — ranked in band,QS ~#82,Australian Year 12 or equivalent; A Levels accepted; indicative ATAR around 80,"AAAB predicted (Maths A, Further Maths A, Chemistry A, Physics B)",Yes,IELTS 6.5 overall (6.0 each band),Adelaide University College foundation studies,AUD 50800,AUD 152400,AUD 29710,3,748743,Adelaide University Global Citizens Scholarship / Vice-Chancellor's Scholarship,Typically 15-30% fee remission,Automatic consideration for some awards,Most assess automatically on admission,"AUD 29,710/yr living costs + first-year tuition + return airfare (subclass 500, 2026 figure)","485 Temporary Graduate visa — 2 yrs for a bachelor; Adelaide is a designated regional centre, which can add an extra year","MQA recognised; solid Malaysian employer recognition, below Go8 peers",Direct to Adelaide University (international),,2027 Semester 2 (July) — Semester 1 (Feb 2027) also offered,"STRUCTURAL CAVEAT: the University of Adelaide and UniSA merged into 'Adelaide University' for 2026 intake, so rankings, course codes and fee schedules are all in flux — anything quoted here is less stable than the other rows and needs re-verifying at Stage 4 against the new entity. Adelaide's regional-centre status is a quiet plus for his migration intent (a possible third year on the 485). Fee is the low end of the quoted A$50,800-94,500 undergraduate band.",https://www.adelaide.edu.au/degree-finder/,Not verified
Finalist,94,A,Match,,National University of Singapore,BSc (Hons) in Data Science and Applied AI,Singapore,Singapore,QS Data Science & AI #3 in the world (2026) — the best-ranked university outside the US,QS #8,"International A-Level accepted. You apply to the Faculty of Science (College of Humanities and Sciences), and declare Data Science and Applied AI as your major after you are admitted — it is not a direct-admit course. You need a very good pass in Maths/Further Maths to take the first-year core; without it you must take the MA1301 bridging course. NUS's published grade profile for the Humanities and Sciences entry route runs from ABB/C at the 10th percentile to AAA/A at the 90th.","AAAB predicted (Maths A, Further Maths A, Chemistry A, Physics B)",Yes,IELTS 6.5 typical for NUS — confirm the exact band at Stage 4,None needed — he clears the published 10th-percentile bar for the Humanities and Sciences entry route,SGD 18050,SGD 72200,SGD 16000,4,476700,ASEAN Undergraduate Scholarship — there is no separate application. Every eligible admission applicant is automatically considered.,"100% of the subsidised tuition fee (the fee that remains after the MOE Tuition Grant), plus S$5,800 a year living allowance, S$3,000 a year accommodation allowance, and a one-off S$1,750 computer allowance.","Selection is by interview, held January to July. NUS states it may award nothing at all if no candidate is good enough. No award count is published, so the real odds are unknown.","Just apply for NUS undergraduate admission by the international-qualifications deadline — you are considered automatically. If shortlisted you are interviewed. You must take up the MOE Tuition Grant to hold the scholarship, and keep a GPA of at least 3.50 to have it renewed each semester. There is no bond from the scholarship itself, but the Tuition Grant you must take carries the 3-year bond.",Proof of funds required for the ICA Student's Pass — amount to confirm at Stage 4,"Singapore has NO post-study work visa. Your Student's Pass lapses when you graduate and you get roughly a 30-day grace period. To stay you need an Employment Pass, which needs a job offer paying at least S$6,000/month from 1 Jan 2027 (non-financial sectors; S$6,600 in financial services) plus enough COMPASS points. Separately, taking the MOE Tuition Grant BONDS you to work for a Singapore-registered company for 3 years after graduating.","MQA recognised; Data Science is not a regulated profession, so no professional-body gate. NUS carries exceptionally strong employer recognition in Malaysia.",NUS Office of Admissions online application (international qualifications route),,"August 2027 — Singapore runs one intake a year, so his 'Sept 2027' maps here cleanly","THE COURSE NAME CHANGED: 'Data Science and Analytics (DSA)' is superseded by 'Data Science and Applied AI (DSAAI)' for cohorts 2026/27 onward — he would be a 2027/28 entrant, so DSAAI is his course. Aggregators still list the old DSA name. FEE TIER: S$18,050 is the ASEAN international rate WITH the MOE Tuition Grant, from NUS's own fee PDF (Humanities and Sciences row, AY2026/27 new students). NUS charges ASEAN citizens LESS than other internationals (S$21,400) — Malaysia qualifies. Without the Tuition Grant the same course is S$36,650/yr, roughly double. Fees are cohort-based and rise each year, so the AY2027/28 figure will be a little higher — verify at Stage 4. ADMISSIBILITY CAVEAT: the ABB/C-to-AAA/A grade profile is published for Singapore-Cambridge A-Levels, NOT international A-Levels, and NUS caps international places. Treat the Match as an indication, not a measurement — this is the single most important thing to verify at Stage 4. THE DOOR MATTERS: entering via the Faculty of Science is materially easier than the direct-admit data science courses (see the Data Science and Economics row, where the profile is AAA/A at BOTH percentiles).",https://www.stat.nus.edu.sg/education/undergraduate/prospective-student/major-in-data-science-applied-ai/,Not verified
Finalist,94,A,Reach,,Nanyang Technological University,Bachelor of Computing (Hons) in Data Science and Artificial Intelligence,Singapore,Singapore,QS Data Science & AI #4 in the world (2026),QS #12,"International A-Level accepted. NTU asks for good A-Level results and a strong Mathematics foundation; there is a published minimum-subject-requirement list per programme. NTU publishes an Indicative Grade Profile, but it is a PDF that could not be retrieved this session — the exact bar for this course is UNKNOWN.","AAAB predicted (Maths A, Further Maths A, Chemistry A, Physics B)",No,"IELTS/TOEFL not compulsory for A-Level applicants taught in English — NTU lists compulsory English tests only for specific qualifications (Gao Kao, HKDSE, etc.). Confirm at Stage 4.",NUS's Faculty of Science route into Data Science and Applied AI is the softer door into a Singapore data science degree,SGD 18050,SGD 72200,SGD 16000,4,476700,NTU ASEAN Undergraduate Scholarship — considered through the admission application,"Tuition (after the MOE Tuition Grant) plus living and accommodation allowances — confirm exact NTU figures at Stage 4; NUS's equivalent is 100% subsidised tuition + S$5,800/yr living + S$3,000/yr accommodation.",Merit-based with interview. No published award count.,Considered via the undergraduate admission application. Requires taking up the MOE Tuition Grant and its 3-year bond.,Proof of funds required for the ICA Student's Pass — amount to confirm at Stage 4,"No post-study work visa. Student's Pass lapses at graduation (~30-day grace). An Employment Pass needs a job offer at S$6,000+/month from 1 Jan 2027 plus COMPASS points. The MOE Tuition Grant bonds you to a Singapore-registered employer for 3 years.","MQA recognised; Data Science is unregulated, no professional-body gate. NTU is very strongly recognised by Malaysian employers.",NTU online undergraduate application (international qualifications route),,August 2027 — Singapore's single annual intake,"A dedicated 4-year direct-honours DS+AI degree, jointly run by the College of Computing and Data Science and the School of Physical and Mathematical Sciences — the purest course match in Singapore alongside NUS DSAAI. NAME INCONSISTENCY ON NTU'S OWN PAGE: the heading says 'Bachelor of Science (Hons)' while the key-details block says 'Bachelor of Computing' — resolve at Stage 4. FEE TIER: S$18,050 is the ASEAN international rate WITH the MOE Tuition Grant ('All Programmes except those listed below' row, NTU's AY2026 fee table); other internationals pay S$21,400 and the no-grant rate is S$36,350 (non-lab) / S$40,600 (lab). CAUTION — two fetches of NTU's own fee page returned DIFFERENT column labels for these numbers; the S$18,050/S$21,400 pair is trusted because it matches NUS's fee PDF exactly (MOE sets the subsidised tiers), but re-read this table at Stage 4. ENTRY MARGIN IS A GUESS, NOT A MEASUREMENT: NTU's IGP PDF was not retrieved, so the Reach call is inferred from NUS's saturated profiles for equivalent direct-admit computing courses. This is the weakest admissibility read on the Singapore rows. Living cost from NTU's own estimate (S$970-S$1,725/month).",https://www.ntu.edu.sg/spms/admissions/undergrad/detail/bachelor-of-science-in-data-science-artificial-intelligence,Not verified
Finalist,91,A,Reach,,National University of Singapore,BSc (Hons) in Data Science and Economics,Singapore,Singapore,QS Data Science & AI #3 in the world (2026),QS #8,Direct-admit course. NUS's published grade profile is AAA/A at BOTH the 10th and the 90th percentile — meaning essentially everyone admitted holds straight A's. Strong Maths required.,"AAAB predicted (Maths A, Further Maths A, Chemistry A, Physics B)",No,IELTS 6.5 typical for NUS — confirm the exact band at Stage 4,"The Faculty of Science route into Data Science and Applied AI is the realistic alternative door — same university, far softer published grade profile",SGD 18050,SGD 72200,SGD 16000,4,476700,ASEAN Undergraduate Scholarship — no separate application; all eligible admission applicants are considered automatically.,"100% of the subsidised tuition fee (after the MOE Tuition Grant), plus S$5,800/yr living allowance, S$3,000/yr accommodation allowance and a one-off S$1,750 computer allowance.","Interview-based, January to July. NUS may award nothing if no candidate is strong enough. No award count published.",Automatic consideration on your admission application; interview if shortlisted. Requires taking the MOE Tuition Grant (and its 3-year bond) and a GPA of 3.50 to renew.,Proof of funds required for the ICA Student's Pass — amount to confirm at Stage 4,"No post-study work visa. Student's Pass lapses at graduation (~30-day grace). An Employment Pass needs a job offer at S$6,000+/month from 1 Jan 2027 plus COMPASS points. The MOE Tuition Grant bonds you to a Singapore-registered employer for 3 years.","MQA recognised; Data Science is unregulated, no professional-body gate. Very strong employer recognition in Malaysia.",NUS Office of Admissions online application (international qualifications route),,August 2027 — Singapore's single annual intake,"THE TRADING-HOBBY FIT: this is the closest match on his whole list to the 'Trading' interest in his profile — data science fused with economics. But it is a REACH and the reason is unusually stark: NUS publishes AAA/A at BOTH the 10th and 90th percentile, which means the grade profile has no spread at all — the course is so oversubscribed that near-everyone admitted has straight A's. His predicted AAAB (a B in Physics) sits below that bar. FEE TIER: S$18,050 is the ASEAN rate WITH the MOE Tuition Grant (Humanities and Sciences row, NUS's own AY2026/27 PDF); the no-grant rate is S$36,650/yr. Grade profile is for Singapore-Cambridge A-Levels, not international A-Levels — indicative only. Worth keeping ON the list as the aspirational NUS door, with Data Science and Applied AI as the realistic one.",https://www.stat.nus.edu.sg/education/undergraduate/prospective-student/major-in-data-science-economics/,Official page
Shortlist,91,A,Reach,,National University of Singapore,Bachelor of Computing (Hons) in Business Analytics,Singapore,Singapore,QS Data Science & AI #3 in the world (2026),QS #8,Direct-admit course in the School of Computing. Published grade profile is AAA/A at both the 10th and 90th percentile. Strong Maths required.,"AAAB predicted (Maths A, Further Maths A, Chemistry A, Physics B)",No,IELTS 6.5 typical for NUS — confirm the exact band at Stage 4,"The Faculty of Science route into Data Science and Applied AI — same university, much softer published grade profile",SGD 18050,SGD 72200,SGD 16000,4,476700,ASEAN Undergraduate Scholarship — no separate application; automatic consideration on the admission application.,"100% of subsidised tuition (after the MOE Tuition Grant), plus S$5,800/yr living, S$3,000/yr accommodation, S$1,750 one-off computer allowance.","Interview-based, January to July; NUS may decline to award. No published award count.",Automatic on the admission application; interview if shortlisted. Requires the MOE Tuition Grant (3-year bond) and GPA 3.50 to renew.,Proof of funds required for the ICA Student's Pass — amount to confirm at Stage 4,"No post-study work visa. Student's Pass lapses at graduation (~30-day grace). Employment Pass needs a job at S$6,000+/month from 1 Jan 2027 plus COMPASS points. The MOE Tuition Grant bonds you to a Singapore-registered employer for 3 years.","MQA recognised; unregulated field, no professional-body gate. Very strong employer recognition in Malaysia.",NUS Office of Admissions online application (international qualifications route),,August 2027 — Singapore's single annual intake,"The applied/business-facing analytics option, and a fit for his stated 'corporate job with good work-life balance' goal. Same Reach problem as Data Science and Economics: the published profile is AAA/A at both percentiles (no spread), and his B in Physics sits below it. FEE TIER: S$18,050 is the ASEAN rate WITH the MOE Tuition Grant — note this is the Computing row of NUS's fee PDF, where the NO-grant rate is S$39,700/yr (higher than the Science faculty's S$36,650), though the with-grant ASEAN rate is identical. Grade profile is Singapore-Cambridge, not international A-Level — indicative only. Included to show the School of Computing door alongside the Science door; if he only keeps one NUS Reach, Data Science and Economics is the better fit for his trading interest.",https://www.nus.edu.sg/oam/admissions/indicative-grade-profile,Not verified
Longlist,70,B,Match,,Singapore Management University,BSc (Economics) with second major in Data Science and Analytics,Singapore,Singapore,"Not ranked by QS for Data Science & AI; SMU is well regarded regionally for business, economics and finance","QS #500s overall — SMU is a small specialist university, so its overall rank understates its standing in business and finance",International A-Level accepted. SMU is less grade-saturated than NUS/NTU but publishes no Indicative Grade Profile — the exact bar is unknown.,"AAAB predicted (Maths A, Further Maths A, Chemistry A, Physics B)",Yes,Confirm at Stage 4,,SGD 25150,SGD 100600,SGD 18000,4,604100,SMU undergraduate scholarships — confirm which are open to international students at Stage 4,Not established this session,Not established this session,Not established this session — SMU's scholarship structure was not confirmed and must not be assumed to match NUS/NTU's ASEAN Undergraduate Scholarship,Proof of funds required for the ICA Student's Pass — amount to confirm at Stage 4,"No post-study work visa. Student's Pass lapses at graduation (~30-day grace). Employment Pass needs a job at S$6,000+/month from 1 Jan 2027 (S$6,600 in financial services, which is where SMU's pipeline points) plus COMPASS points. The MOE Tuition Grant bonds you to a Singapore-registered employer for 3 years.","MQA recognised; unregulated field, no professional-body gate. SMU is well recognised by Malaysian employers in banking and finance.",SMU online undergraduate application (international qualifications),,August 2027 — Singapore's single annual intake,"THE HONEST CATCH: Data Science and Analytics at SMU is a SECOND MAJOR bolted onto an Economics degree, not a data science degree in its own right — that is why course_match is 3 and not 5. This is the same trade-off shape as the US liberal-arts rows: strong on fit-to-his-interests and city/industry access, weak on being the actual thing he said he wants. THE UPSIDE: SMU is downtown, seminar-taught, internship-heavy, and feeds Singapore's banking and trading floors — the best structural fit on his entire list for the 'Trading' hobby in his profile. FEE TIER: S$25,150 is SMU's ASEAN rate WITH the MOE Tuition Grant — materially higher than NUS/NTU's S$18,050 (other internationals S$26,200; no-grant S$47,700). Living estimate raised to S$18,000 because SMU is city-centre with no real campus housing — this figure is an estimate, not an SMU number. NAME-COLLISION TRAP HIT THIS SESSION: 'SMU' also means Southern Methodist University in Dallas, Texas — a Firecrawl scrape of datascience.smu.edu returned the TEXAS university's fees. Anything sourced from smu.edu (not smu.edu.sg) is the wrong SMU.",https://economics.smu.edu.sg/bachelor-science-economics/curriculum/2nd-major-data-science-and-analytics,Not verified
Longlist,54,C,Safety,,James Cook University Singapore,Bachelor of Science (Majoring in Data Science),Singapore,Singapore,Not ranked by QS for Data Science & AI,JCU (the Australian parent) sits around QS #400-500; the Singapore branch campus carries little independent standing,Open entry relative to the public universities — his AAAB is comfortably above what JCU Singapore asks. Preparatory Maths/Chemistry subjects can be waived with relevant A-Level results.,"AAAB predicted (Maths A, Further Maths A, Chemistry A, Physics B)",Yes,IELTS 6.0 with no component below 6.0 (official JCU Singapore page),,SGD 35839,SGD 71678,SGD 16000,2,362873,JCU Singapore scholarships — not established this session,Not established this session,Not established this session,"NOT eligible for the MOE Tuition Grant or the ASEAN Undergraduate Scholarship — those are for Singapore's autonomous universities (NUS/NTU/SMU/SUTD/SIT/SUSS), not private institutions. The listed fee is the full fee with no subsidy available.",Proof of funds required for the ICA Student's Pass — amount to confirm at Stage 4,"No post-study work visa, and NO Tuition Grant bond either (the grant is not available here) — so no obligation to stay, but also no subsidy. An Employment Pass still needs a job at S$6,000+/month from 1 Jan 2027 plus COMPASS points, and a 2-year branch-campus degree is a weaker COMPASS profile than an NUS/NTU one.","MQA recognition of a 2-year JCU Singapore BSc is NOT established and must be checked — this is a real open question, not a formality. Data Science is unregulated so there is no professional-body gate, but a 2-year bachelor's is unusual by Malaysian norms.",JCU Singapore direct online application,,"September 2027 (JCU runs trimesters: January, May, September) — the only Singapore row that actually offers a September start","THE DURATION INVERSION — the mirror image of the Australian honours trap: this bachelor's runs 24 MONTHS full-time, not 3-4 years, because JCU Singapore teaches three trimesters a year. That is what makes it the cheapest row on his entire list (~S$71,678 total tuition is JCU's own published whole-course figure, incl. GST, NOT an annual fee — the annual_tuition here is that total divided by 2 and is a derived number, not a quoted one). THE TRADE-OFF IS BRUTAL AND IT LANDS ON HIS #1 PRIORITY: this is his only Singapore Safety, and it is unranked for data science. He said he values 'Experience and the name'. JCU Singapore has the experience and none of the name. Keep it on the list as the honest floor — do not inflate it, do not quietly drop it. TWO REAL CHECKS FOR STAGE 4: (1) MQA recognition of a 2-year BSc; (2) whether a 2-year degree is accepted for Employment Pass COMPASS qualification points.",https://www.jcu.edu.sg/courses-and-study/courses/course/bachelor-of-science-majoring-in-data-science,Not verified
Longlist,79,A,Safety,,Monash University Malaysia,Bachelor of Applied Data Science,Malaysia,Subang Jaya,Monash (parent) QS Data Science & AI top-100; strong subject rep,Monash QS ~#37 (parent university),A-Level aggregate score 9 (Monash MY scale); higher-level Mathematics required,"A/A/B/A predicted (Maths A, Further Maths A, Physics B, Chemistry A)",Yes,Monash English requirements (IELTS ~6.5 typical); MUET accepted for locals,MUFY (Monash University Foundation Year) if below A-Level bar,MYR 51360,MYR 154080,MYR 15000,3,199080,Monash Malaysia merit / High Achiever scholarships — apply via admissions,,,,"n/a (Malaysian citizen, local student)",Graduates in Malaysia — no automatic foreign PSW visa; Monash testamur is globally portable for later overseas job/visa applications,MQA-registered (baseline); Monash degree strongly recognised by Malaysian employers,Direct application (Monash Malaysia admissions),,2027 (intakes Feb / Jul / Oct — NO Sept intake),"FLAGGED THREAD RESOLVED: fully in Malaysia, 3 yrs, NOT a mandatory 2+2 to Clayton (credit transfer is optional prior-learning only). A cheaper local route to a Monash degree (cf. the Clayton Applied Data Science row already on his list). Dedicated Applied Data Science degree — best local course_match. Intakes Feb/Jul/Oct, so 'Sept 2027' won't map — settle intake at Stage 4. Recognition scored on real standing, NOT MQA (DS is unregulated, no EAC/ETAC ladder).",https://www.monash.edu.my/study/undergraduate/science/bachelor-of-applied-data-science,Not verified
