Longlist,75,A,Match,,University of Malaya (UM),Bachelor of Computer Science (Data Science),Malaysia,Kuala Lumpur,UM is Malaysia's top public university for CS/computing,QS #58 world (2026) — highest-ranked Malaysian university,A-Level: grade B in Mathematics + grade B in one of Physics/Computing/Chemistry/Biology/Further Mathematics,A/A/B/A predicted — clears B/B comfortably,Yes,MUET Band 3.5 (local route) / IELTS 5.5 equivalent,UM ASASI (foundation) as alternative entry,MYR 21571,MYR 75500,MYR 15000,3.5,128000,UPU subsidised place is itself the main funding lever for a local student; limited merit scholarships for SATU self-funded route,,,,n/a (local student),Graduates in Malaysia — no automatic foreign PSW; UM degree well recognised by Malaysian employers,MQA-registered (baseline); UM carries the strongest domestic employer recognition of the local publics,UPU (subsidised) or SATU (direct self-funded local entry),,2027 (Semester 1 October / Semester 2 March intakes),"TWO FEE ROUTES: RM75,500 is the SATU direct self-funded LOCAL fee (used here). Via UPU the subsidised public rate is far lower (~RM15k for the whole degree) but is a competitive channel-based allocation — the SATU fee 'is not applicable for UPU applicant'. Verify the dedicated Data Science track vs the Information Systems track at Stage 4 (the scraped page was the IS track, which shares the B/B A-Level bar). Highest 'name' among local publics. Entry bar is modest but UM is competitive/oversubscribed for computing — scored Match, leaning Safety.",https://study.um.edu.my/,Not verified
